Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dotfiles/notmuch: Keep quarantined mail out of the inbox
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: sxkzwvlrqmynzyywlwwwoukzmyspmntu
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:05:28 +0000

lab-process-mail answers whatever is tagged inbox, and the inbox tag
is recomputed on every notmuch new, so nothing short of a reply keeps
a message out of it. A message from a sender the agent must not act on
needs to leave the inbox without being answered, and for every reader,
not just the one who set it aside.

Filing its file under the quarantine/ maildir does that. The tag comes
from where the file lives, so it lives in the mail branch like every
other derived tag, a rebuilt database gets it back from notmuch new
alone, and moving the file back out undoes it.
---
change-id: sxkzwvlrqmynzyywlwwwoukzmyspmntu

 dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh b/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh
index 269caaff..72f06910 100755
--- a/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh
+++ b/dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh
@@ -2,16 +2,19 @@
 #
 # mail-tag.sh -- derive notmuch tags from the contents of the list.
 #
-# The sent, inbox and replied tags are recomputed from the messages on
-# every run, so the database holds no state of its own: rebuild it from
-# the maildir and the same tags come back.
+# The sent, inbox, replied and quarantined tags are recomputed from the
+# messages on every run, so the database holds no state of its own:
+# rebuild it from the maildir and the same tags come back.
 #
 #   sent     from the user (notmuch user.primary_email or other_email)
 #   inbox    from someone else, and the user has not replied to it
 #   replied  from someone else, and the user has replied to it
+#   quarantined  filed under quarantine/; never in the inbox
 #
 # "Replied to" means a message from the user names it in In-Reply-To.
-# Drafts get none of these tags.
+# lab-process-mail quarantines a message from a sender it does not act
+# on by moving its file, unchanged, into the quarantine/ maildir, and
+# moving it back undoes it. Drafts get none of these tags.
 #
 # Runs from the notmuch post-new hook, so notmuch new applies it.
 
@@ -19,6 +22,7 @@ set -eu
 set -o pipefail
 
 readonly drafts='path:drafts/**'
+readonly quarantine='path:quarantine/**'
 
 main() {
 	local me id
@@ -31,6 +35,8 @@ main() {
 		replied_ids "${me}" | while read -r id; do
 			echo "+replied -inbox -- id:\"${id}\" and not (${me}) and not ${drafts}"
 		done
+		echo "-quarantined -- not ${quarantine}"
+		echo "+quarantined -inbox -- ${quarantine}"
 	} | notmuch tag --batch
 }
 
